    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d21-a7">

                <pb facs="0130" n="24" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg24"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 7 in No. 183.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Grant to Mr.
                            Janowitz</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-07-09"><hi rendition="#italic">July 9,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Yesterday I called at the ministry of
                    foreign affairs here and placed a written statement of your case in the hands of
                    the minister, who promised me that he would make inquiries into your case by
                    writing to the authorities at Lublo.</p>
                <p>Yours, respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. D. Grant</hi>.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>P. S.—Before I had time to send the foregoing letter to the post-office I
                        received a note from the ministry of foreign affairs, which, translated,
                        reads as follows: [Here follows a copy of inclosure No. 6.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
